{"chunk_id": "2b045aba1adb", "text": "Bharata tells Rama of their father King Dasharatha\u2019s death, and the news strikes Rama like a divine weapon in battle. Overcome with grief, he collapses unconscious, and when revived he laments that he was absent in exile and unable to perform the king\u2019s final rites. He mourns the loss not only of a father but of the moral guide who once instructed him in right and wrong. Turning to duty, Rama performs funeral libations on the sacred Mandakini River with Lakshmana, Bharata, and Sita, offering water and simple forest food to his father\u2019s spirit. Their collective grief echoes through the mountains, drawing the army toward the hermitage. The episode underscores Rama\u2019s filial devotion, the sacred importance of funeral rites, and the emotional cost of exile.\nRama learns of King Dasharatha\u2019s death, collapses in grief, performs water and food rites by the Mandakini, and mourns with his family.\nThemes: filial grief, funeral rites, dharma and duty, exile sorrow, family mourning", "vector": [0.016822073608636856, -0.019209980964660645, -0.011465957388281822, 0.0002801455557346344, -0.009464917704463005, 0.020797472447156906, -0.019196640700101852, -0.006690142676234245, -0.01747574657201767, -0.02011711895465851, 0.0004969248548150063, 0.01923666149377823, 0.0035785259678959846, 0.018462926149368286, -0.01678205281496048, -0.0014399148058146238, 0.03868676722049713, -0.01646188646554947, 0.04100797325372696, -0.006273259408771992, 0.013560378924012184, -0.01654192805290222, 0.006446682848036289, 0.01603499799966812, -0.015848234295845032, 0.003168312832713127, 0.01583489403128624, -0.031189538538455963, 0.018196120858192444, -0.012566529214382172, -0.008117550984025002, -0.030175678431987762, 0.0016083356458693743, -0.017889294773340225, -0.012639900669455528, 0.003511824645102024, -0.0067134881392121315, -0.019917014986276627, 0.007577270269393921, -0.00610650610178709, 0.0077573638409376144, -0.0127266123890876